# Git: Commit And Push By Default

When you finish **any** coherent change (large or small)—feature slice, refactor, UX, data tweaks, fixes—finish with a **git commit and `git push`** by default.

**Do not commit or push only if** the user explicitly asks to skip Git for _this task_ or says not to push.

Use a clear conventional-style message summarizing intent. Never force-push to `main`/`master`; never destructive git unless the user explicitly requests it.
